   "title_cn": "南苏丹伦拜克北部：两兄弟因山羊纠纷互相开枪身亡",
   "title_original": "Rumbek North: Two brothers shoot each other dead in goat dispute",
   "summary_cn": "南苏丹湖泊州伦拜克北部县发生一起枪击事件，两兄弟因一只山羊的归属纠纷互相开枪，双双当场死亡。一名家族长老向Radio Tamazuj表示，两人此前曾因一头牛发生争执，经家族成员和长老调解后达成协议，但纠纷再度激化。当地社区组织CEPO谴责该事件，呼吁通过对话解决纠纷，并敦促政府调查。",
   "summary_original": "Two brothers have shot and killed each other during a dispute over ownership of a The post Rumbek North: Two brothers shoot each other dead in goat dispute appeared first on Radio Tamazuj .",
   "event_time": "2026-09-27T10:27:26Z",
   "published_time": "2026-09-27T10:27:26Z",
   "location": "",
   "china_related": false,
   "verification_level": "single_source",
   "verification_label_cn": "单一来源",
   "independent_source_count": 1,
   "source_links": [
    {
     "url": "https://www.radiotamazuj.org/en/news/article/rumbek-north-two-brothers-shoot-each-other-dead-in-goat-dispute",
     "source_name": "Radio Tamazuj",
     "source_group": "ssd",
     "language": "en"
    }
   ],
   "potential_impact": "",
   "progress": "",
   "current_policy_passed": true,
   "quality_gate_passed": true,
   "legacy_migration_preserved": false,
   "legacy_visibility": true,
   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "Two brothers have shot and killed each other during a dispute over ownership of a goat in Rumbek North County, Lakes State, according to a family elder.\nThe incident happened on Thursday after the brothers exchanged gunfire during an argument, Santino Adong Keloktuol, a former state minister for culture, youth and sports and a relative of the men, told Radio Tamazuj.\nAdong said the brothers had previously disagreed over a cow, but the dispute was resolved by family members and elders without anyone being injured.\nUnder the agreement, the elder brother was to give the cow to his younger brother, while the younger brother agreed to compensate him with a goat.\nAdong said the dispute resurfaced when the elder brother went to ask his younger brother for the goat.\nHe said the younger brother then opened fire, seriously wounding his elder brother, who returned fire. Both men died at the scene.\nAdong rejected claims that the confrontation was linked to a dispute over the inheritance of their late brother’s widow.\nDaniel Laat, the Lakes State coordinator for the Community Empowerment for Progress Organization (CEPO), condemned the incident and urged families and communities to resolve disputes through dialogue.\n“Whenever you have a dispute with your brother over something, there is a need to report it to the family members or the community so that dialogue can be organised,” he said.\nLaat said disputes over property should not escalate into violence, urging young people in particular to seek mediation from family elders and community leaders.\nHe also called on the government to investigate the incident and prevent the dispute from spreading to other family members.\n“We are calling for calm and urging the government to handle such cases and ensure that other people do not do the same,” he said.\nLaat said similar disputes had led to violence among relatives in Lakes State, adding that family and community dialogue could help prevent such incidents.",
