   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "Italy\nA court in Rome on Monday sentenced three Egyptian security officials convicted of aggravated kidnapping in the abduction of an Italian researcher in Cairo to 10 years in prison, while a fourth defendant was acquitted of murder.\nThe ruling marks the most significant judicial milestone yet in the decade-long quest for accountability over Giulio Regeni’s death. Rome's chief prosecutor Francesco Lo Voi welcomed the outcome, saying the verdict was achieved despite what he described as a lack of  “meaningful cooperation”  from Egyptian authorities during the investigation. The defendants were tried in absentia.\n“We are satisfied for having brought the case out of the quagmire into which it had risked sinking,”  Lo Voi told reporters after the verdict.",
