   "body_extracted": "THE Nigerian Consulate-General in Johannesburg has called on South African authorities to investigate the deaths of three Nigerian nationals in separate incidents between September 18 and 21, 2026.\nThe Consulate made the call in a statement dated September 28 and signed by the Consul-General, Nnikanwa Okey-Uche.\nThe deaths occurred in Bloemfontein, Pretoria and Ekurhuleni, according to the statement.\nFormer Nigerian Minister of Aviation and Nigeria’s High Commissioner to South Africa, Femi Fani-Kayode, who shared the statement on X, said the latest deaths brought to 12 the number of Nigerians he said had been killed in South Africa in 2026.\nFani-Kayode also claimed that 112 Nigerians had been killed in South Africa since 2022, including 32 allegedly killed by members of the country’s security forces.",
