   "body_extracted": "Son of Zambian bishop detained in post-election raid fears for his father's safety\nTo play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser.\nThis video can not be played\nSon of Zambian bishop detained in post-election raid fears for his father's safety       Close\nThe son of detained Zambian opposition politician Bishop Trevor Mwamba has told the BBC he is concerned for his father's safety after the former Bishop of Botswana was detained along with 10 other opposition figures by authorities.\nEno Mwamba said his father, who is leader of the United National Independence Party, has been charged with treason following President Hakainde Hichilema's disputed election victory.\nThe opposition politicians have been held since a raid by security forces on 14 August.\nOpposition leader Brian Mundubile, head of the National Reconciliation Party for Unity and Prosperity (NRPUP), had gone into hiding after disputing the election result, but has since also been detained by the authorities.\nThe government accuses the opposition of planning an armed insurgency and have charged the detained politicians with treason. They have denied the charges.\nProduced, filmed and edited by Aaron Akinyemi\nSubsection\nAfrica\nPublished\n9 hours ago\nShare\nclose panel\nShare page\nCopy link\nAbout sharing\nRelated topics\nZambia                Follow   Zambia\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nZambia\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in   My News   and in a collection on the   News homepage .\nAfrica                Follow   Africa\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nAfrica\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in   My News   and in a collection on the   News homepage .\nRead description",
