   "body_extracted": "Defence/Security  Fire service warns FCT residents against walking, driving through floodwaters\nFire service warns FCT residents against walking, driving through floodwaters\nBy  isaac aregbesola   ·   2 minutes ago   ·  2 min read\n✓\n✓\nBy Kelechi Ogunleye\nThe Federal Fire Service (FFS) FCT Command has advised residents to desist from walking or driving through floodwaters as rainfall intensifies.\nThe FFS FCT command Public Relations Officer (PRO), Barnabas Anyam, warned that the temptation to hurriedly cross floods posed great risks to live.\nAnyam noted that even shallow water on roads could pose serious danger to lives and property.\n“Residents caught in floods are advised to remain calm and move immediately to higher ground,” he advised.\nThe spokesperson advised residents to keep children away from floodwaters and open culverts as well as to move valuables, important documents, food supplies and other essential items to higher levels in due time.\nHe also warned against living electrical appliances on in homes during rainfalls, stressing that all sockets should be switched off.\nHe further said that evacuation of children, elderly persons and persons with disabilities should be prioritised during household floods, and urged residents to avoid drinking or using potentially contaminated floodwater.\nAnyam reaffirmed the command’s commitment to responding swiftly to emergencies and safeguarding lives and property across the territory.\nHe quoted the command’s Controller, Muhammed Anas, as appealing to residents to cooperate with emergency responders, obey safety instructions and promptly report flood incidents and other emergencies to the appropriate authorities.\nAnas urged residents to call the  FFS FCT emergency contact number – 0803 200 3557 in case of emergencies.(NAN)\nEdited by Deborah Coker\n✓\n✓\nTags:    driving through floodwaters\nFire service warns FCT residents against walking\nisaac aregbesola",
