   "publication_reason": "Stage 3B 真实采集",
   "body_extracted": "ONE of the parents of prospective National Youth Service Corps (NYSC) members who were abducted while travelling to orientation camps on Nigeria’s Independence Day has appealed to President Bola Tinubu to intervene in their rescue.\nThe incident occurred at about 6:30 a.m. on Thursday, October 1, along the Owerri-Onitsha Road near Umunoha, Imo State, when two buses conveying the prospective NYSC members and other passengers came under attack by suspected gunmen.\nThe Imo State Police Command confirmed the attack and said it had deployed tactical teams and operational assets, in collaboration with other security agencies, to rescue the abducted passengers and arrest the suspected attackers.\nThe command said both buses had been recovered and 10 victims rescued at the scene.\nHowever, the police said the exact number of persons whisked away by the assailants was still being verified.",
